     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've processed all five items. I sent Isla one message and logged the run.\n\n- **Fergus's bookings:** I recorded Fergus as stewarding Glen Dunnock and Kinloch-on-Spey, because Isla had approved both in her console. I didn't record Kirsty's pencilling at Glen Dunnock. Isla had already made that change by hand.\n- **Senga:** She can't do Kinloch-on-Spey, so I recorded a No there and a Yes for the other five games.\n- **Fergus's dates:** He said he'll be at the setup day, which was already a Yes.\n- **Bridie Tosh:** Senga suggested her for the children's races. I proposed her for the Pipeline, and the message asks Isla to approve her in the console.\n- **Briefing mail:** The mail about the 24 June briefing isn't an availability statement, so I made no change for it.\n\nThe Saturday 10 July games (Balvaig Bridge and Inverallt) are still Red, short 2 across the day. Kinloch-on-Spey looks Green with Senga out. There were no engine changes to pass on."
     }
